---Template specifying rules for generating shifts. A shift is a unit of work that specifies a start time, end time, and may contain events (e.g. lunch, breaks etc.). Shifts will be assigned to specific dates in the response.
---@class gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.ShiftTemplate
---@field assignableEmployeeIds? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.StringList Optional. A list of specific employee IDs that can be assigned to shifts generated by this template. If this field is present, there will be `EmployeeSchedule`s in the response for which the `EmployeeSchedule.employee_id` field is set to one of the IDs in this list. The number of employee schedules with an assigned employee ID will be between `minimum_employee_count` and `maximum_employee_count`. If this field is empty, between `minimum_employee_count` and `maximum_employee_count` employees can be assigned to shifts generated by this template and the employee schedules won't have an assigned employee ID. Currently, only one assignable employee ID is supported.
---@field minimumIntereventGapMinutes? number Optional. Minimum minutes between the end of one event and the start of the next.
---@field eventTemplates? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.EventTemplateList Optional. Rules for generating events for each shift. Exactly one event will be included in each shift for each `EventTemplate` specified.
---@field startTimeIncrementMinutes? number Optional. The time increment (in minutes) used to generate the set of possible start times between `earliest_start_time` and `latest_start_time`. For example, if the earliest start time is 8:00, the latest start time is 8:30, and the start time increment is 10 minutes, then all possible start times for this shift template are: 8:00, 8:10, 8:20, and 8:30.
---@field daysOffDates? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.DateList Optional. Fixed dates when shifts from this template should not be generated.
---@field maximumEmployeeCount? number Required. Maximum number of employees that can be assigned to all shifts generated by this template on working days.
---@field earliestStartTime? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.TimeOfDay Required. Earliest time in the day that a shift can start. This value is specified with hours and minutes; seconds and nanos are ignored.
---@field id? string Required. Unique ID of this template.
---@field daysOffCountPerWeek? number Optional. Fixed number of days off per week. An employee has a given day off if they are not assigned to a shift that starts on that day. A week is 7 days and begins on Sunday.
---@field minimumEmployeeCount? number Optional. Minimum number of employees that can be assigned to all shifts generated by this template on working days.
---@field latestStartTime? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.TimeOfDay Required. Latest time in the day that a shift can start. This value is specified with hours and minutes; seconds and nanos are ignored. If this value is less than the `earliest_start_time`, it may imply an overnight shift.
---@field durationMinutes? number Required. Fixed duration of a shift generated by this template.

---@alias gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.ShiftTemplateList gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.ShiftTemplate[]

---Specifies additional parameters for the solver generating shifts.
---@class gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.SolverConfig
---@field scheduleType? gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.SolverConfigScheduleTypeEnum|string Required. Specifies the type of schedule to generate.
---@field maximumProcessingDuration? string Optional. Maximum time the solver should spend on the problem. If not set, defaults to 1 minute. The choice of a time limit should depend on the size of the problem. To give an example, when solving a 7-day instance with 2 `ShiftTemplates`, each with ~20 possible start times and holding 2 events with ~30 possible start times, and two days off per week, recommended values are: <10s for fast solutions (and likely suboptimal), (10s, 300s) for good quality solutions, and >300s for an exhaustive search. Larger instances may require longer time limits. This value is not a hard limit and it does not account for the communication overhead. The expected latency to solve the problem may slightly exceed this value.

---@alias gcp.contactcenteraiplatform_v1alpha1.SolverConfigScheduleTypeEnum "SCHEDULE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SINGLE_SHIFT"|"WEEKLY_WITH_FIXED_EVENTS"|"WEEKLY_WITH_VARIABLE_EVENTS"

